---
import Poem from "../components/Poem.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Page.astro";

const GAMES_LIST = [
  {
    title: "Skyrim",
    steam:
      "https://store.steampowered.com/app/489830/The_Elder_Scrolls_V_Skyrim_Special_Edition/",
    description:
      "My all-time favorite game. I have Akatosh tattooed on my leg. What more can I say?",
    rating: "10/10",
  },
  {
    title: "Hollow Knight",
    steam: "https://store.steampowered.com/app/367520/Hollow_Knight/",
    description:
      "Hollow Knight is a treasure. It's an exercise in futility, yet also a meditation on what it means to be alive. The game challenges you fairly, and those challenges are always rewarded with stunning beauty.",
    rating: "10/10",
  },
  {
    title: "Elden Ring",
    steam: "https://store.steampowered.com/app/1245620/ELDEN_RING/",
    description:
      "I'm a sucker for all things Souls-related. I played Demon's Souls back in 2010 and every Dark Souls title in between.",
    rating: "10/10",
  },
  {
    title: "Sekiro: Shadows Die Twice",
    steam:
      "https://store.steampowered.com/app/814380/Sekiro_Shadows_Die_Twice__GOTY_Edition/",
    description:
      "Honestly, I don't know if I like Elden Ring or Sekiro more. And in many ways, it isn't even fair to compare the two, despite being made by the same people.",
    rating: "10/10",
  },
  {
    title: "Stardew Valley",
    steam: "https://store.steampowered.com/app/413150/Stardew_Valley/",
    description:
      "I can't pass up a hat-tip to this one. Stardew Valley holds a special place in my heart, if not for me, then for all the wonderful people I know who are so enamored by the game.",
    rating: "9/10",
  },
];

const BOOKS_LIST = [
  {
    title: "The Name of the Wind",
    goodReads:
      "https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/186074.The_Name_of_the_Wind",
    description:
      "Inspiration is something I strive to find only through serendipity. Forcing such a delicate thing would push it away, like magnets of the same pole. When I read The Name of the Wind, I had heard about it, been told of its worth. But I gave it no expectations. And that is when inspiration flitted into existence like a fae phasing between worlds. I cannot recommend this book enough.",
  },
  {
    title: "House of Leaves",
    goodReads: "https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/24800.House_of_Leaves",
    description:
      "I'll be honest. I care about complexity. It thrills me when something wends, makes me question my understanding of the world, and House of Leaves did exactly that. The story—or, rather, stories—interleave philosophy, poetry, and text-book-esque prose in a way that made me strive to be a better person. Yes, it's fiction. But in the words of Tom Spanbaur: Fiction is the lie that tells the truth truer.",
  },
];
---
<Layout
  title="Hobbies & Interests"
  description="Poetry, favorite games, books, and fantasy worlds from Isiah Fletcher's personal archive."
>
  <div class="hobbies-library">
    <section class="library-intro" aria-labelledby="library-heading">
      <p class="section-label">A personal collection</p>
      <h2 id="library-heading">Worlds worth wandering.</h2>
      <div class="intro-columns">
        <p>I love narrative. It <em>excites me</em> to sink my teeth into the flesh of a different world. From Dungeons & Dragons to copious video games, anime to books, it's how I've come to even perceive our own world: a story in which I am one of trillions of characters.</p>
        <p>Unashamedly, I love Medieval Fantasy over everything else. Whether that's the narratives I consume, or Renaissance Fairs (yes, I cosplay a fantasy character. Come at me), I yearn to live as if it were all real. Of course, modernity has its perks. I am a software engineer. I know full well video games wouldn't have existed if it weren't for progress. Yet that's the beauty of the modern age! Our choices are near-limitless.</p>
      </div>
      <nav class="library-index" aria-label="Explore interests">
        <a href="#poetry"><span>01</span> Poetry <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href="#games"><span>02</span> Video games <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href="#books"><span>03</span> Books <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </nav>
    </section>
    <section class="library-section" id="poetry" aria-labelledby="poetry-heading">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-label">01 / Original writing</p><h2 id="poetry-heading">Poetry</h2></div><p>When I'm not writing or reading fantasy stories, coding or working out at the gym, I'm writing poetry. Here are a few pieces from the archive.</p></div>
    <div class="poetry-grid">
      <Poem
        title="The Act of Giving"
        body={[
          "Blood cradles the shoreline",
          "where my visage skitters",
          "in the firelight behind",
          "like dawn moonbeams. I heave,",
          "reel my battered self",
          "upward, a hunter",
          "(a prey) no longer to this",
          "eventuality—ready now",
          "to nourish, disseminate",
          "the rhythm of nurtured words",
          "that drum my final heartbeats:",
          null,
          "peace, at last, is listening",
          "to the ash patter on",
          "the crests of scattered waves.",
        ]}
      />
      <Poem
        title="On Letting"
        body={[
          "A dream of honey sweetness",
          "is a dream I know",
          "in which I love,",
          "the venesection",
          "purifies the mind-murmurs",
          "and grave memories.",
          null,
          "The boy who is no longer",
          "afraid of troll's",
          "blood mourns his own",
          "passing, funeral",
          "blessed by rain, laughter:",
          "let him be slowly",
          "consumed by lichen,",
          "moss, blood-forged love",
          "in the hardship of friendship,",
          "and let his dreams be grounded,",
          "sorrow answered in the echoes",
          "between mountains, and apologies",
          "held softly as a crying child",
          null,
          "then released like wistful",
          "wind. He, to the moment,",
          "here only",
          "as breath bargains",
          "with the interstice. Here,",
          null,
          "fear and sorrow",
          "safeguard temples,",
          "bow deep in deference",
          "to antediluvian deities:",
          "Let them serve a reminder",
          "of the magic that heals",
          "all laid barren the past.",
        ]}
      />

      <Poem
        title="In Recurse"
        body={[
          "Memory is a meteor shower",
          "and galaxy black is an empty",
          "oblivion if in-betweens",
          "are seen as something",
          "discarded, distant from all,",
          "but is emptiness anything",
          "besides anticipation,",
          "a seed that flowers into",
          null,
          "joy? A small streak ignites",
          "the thought of a flurry",
          "of fur unfurling",
          "when you stretch your loving",
          "body across my lap,",
          "and the impact...",
          "well, that's the easy part:",
          "when the last thing I saw",
          "was your love limp",
          "and cold as a starless sky,",
          "and the emptiness it created",
          "when I knew I did not fill",
          "each moment with precious",
          null,
          "joy. But to you, it wasn't",
          "a thing to fill or discard,",
          "but who you were. Joy becoming",
          "itself. You were the sky",
          "across galaxies, and you,",
          "too, became a prediction",
          "in the art of loving,",
          "until all that was",
          "and all that is",
          "is a unanimous pulse",
          "in anticipation",
          "of dawn.",
        ]}
      />
    </div>


    </section>
    <section class="library-section" id="games" aria-labelledby="games-heading">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-label">02 / Interactive worlds</p><h2 id="games-heading">Video games</h2></div><p>The games I enjoy most.</p></div>
      <div class="game-grid">
        {GAMES_LIST.map((game,index) => (
          <article class="game-card">
            <div class="card-top"><span class="item-number">{String(index+1).padStart(2,"0")}</span><span class="rating">{game.rating}</span></div>
            <h3>{game.title}</h3>
            <p>{game.description}</p>
            <a href={game.steam} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View on Steam ↗</a>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="library-section" id="books" aria-labelledby="books-heading">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-label">03 / On the shelf</p><h2 id="books-heading">Books</h2></div><p>A couple of stories that stayed with me.</p></div>
      <div class="book-grid">
        {BOOKS_LIST.map((book,index) => (
          <article class="book-card">
            <div class="book-spine" aria-hidden="true"><span>{String(index+1).padStart(2,"0")}</span></div>
            <div class="book-content">
              <p class="section-label">From the bookshelf</p>
              <h3>{book.title}</h3>
              <p>{book.description}</p>
              <a href={book.goodReads} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Find on Goodreads ↗</a>
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
<style>
  .hobbies-library{--library-border:#566b5d;--library-sage:#a9c1a3;--library-paper:#e2d7bb}
  .library-intro{padding:0 0 2.8rem}
  .section-label{font:600 .72rem/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.17em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--library-sage)!important;margin:0 0 .9rem}
  .library-intro h2{font-size:clamp(2.8rem,5vw,4.35rem);line-height:1.1;max-width:none;margin:0 0 1.6rem;color:var(--library-paper)}
  .intro-columns{display:block;max-width:70ch}
  .intro-columns p{line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 1.15rem;color:#c3d0bf}
  .intro-columns p:first-child{font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--library-paper)}
  .library-index{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:clamp(1.3rem,3vw,3rem);margin-top:2rem;padding-top:1rem;border-top:1px solid var(--library-border)}
  .library-index a{display:inline-flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:center;padding:.35rem 0;color:var(--library-paper);text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid transparent}
  .library-index a span:first-child{color:var(--library-sage);font:600 .75rem system-ui,sans-serif}
  .library-index a span:last-child{color:var(--library-sage)}
  .library-index a:hover,.library-index a:focus-visible{border-bottom-color:#a9c1a3;color:#a9c1a3}
  .library-section{padding:3.5rem 0 4.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--library-border);scroll-margin-top:2rem}
  .section-heading{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:2rem;align-items:end;margin-bottom:2rem}
  .section-heading h2{font-size:clamp(2.7rem,5vw,4.2rem);margin:0}
  .section-heading>p{max-width:48ch;margin:0 0 .4rem;color:#c3d0bf}
  .poetry-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem;align-items:stretch}
  .poetry-grid :global(.poem){max-width:none;min-width:0;padding:2rem 1.5rem;background:#34443c;border:1px solid #526658;border-top:3px solid #bf8f68;border-radius:3px;box-shadow:0 10px 28px rgba(10,20,16,.12)}
  .poetry-grid :global(.poem-title){font-family:"CormorantGaramond",Georgia,serif;font-size:1.75rem;line-height:1.2;color:#e2d7bb}
  .poetry-grid :global(.poem p){font-size:.99rem;line-height:1.8;color:#d1d9cb}
  .game-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}
  .game-card{background:#34443c;border:1px solid #526658;border-radius:3px;padding:clamp(1.4rem,3vw,2rem);display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-height:270px}
  .card-top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:1.6rem}
  .item-number{font:600 .8rem system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#a9c1a3}
  .rating{display:inline-flex;padding:.25rem .65rem;border:1px solid #6d806f;border-radius:2px;color:#e2d7bb;font:600 .78rem system-ui,sans-serif}
  .game-card h3,.book-card h3{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.5rem);margin:0 0 .9rem;color:#e2d7bb}
  .game-card p,.book-card p{color:#c3d0bf;line-height:1.75}
  .game-card a,.book-card a{margin-top:auto;align-self:flex-start}
  .book-grid{display:grid;gap:1.25rem}
  .book-card{display:grid;grid-template-columns:68px minmax(0,1fr);background:#34443c;border:1px solid #526658;border-radius:3px;overflow:hidden}
  .book-spine{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:#405447;border-right:1px solid #6d806f;color:#bf8f68;font:400 2rem "CormorantGaramond",Georgia,serif}
  .book-content{padding:clamp(1.4rem,3vw,2.4rem);display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start}
  .book-content p:not(.section-label){max-width:75ch}
  .game-card,.book-card,.poetry-grid :global(.poem){transform:perspective(900px) rotateX(var(--tilt-x,0deg)) rotateY(var(--tilt-y,0deg))}
  .game-card,.book-card,.poetry-grid :global(.poem),.library-index a{transition:transform .3s ease,box-shadow .3s ease,border-color .3s ease,background-color .3s ease}
  @media(hover:hover) and (pointer:fine){.game-card:hover,.book-card:hover,.poetry-grid :global(.poem):hover{border-color:#a9c1a3;box-shadow:0 18px 36px rgba(10,20,16,.25)}}
  @media(max-width:850px){.poetry-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
  @media(max-width:650px){.intro-columns,.section-heading,.game-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.library-index{gap:.8rem 1.6rem}.poetry-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.library-section{padding:2.7rem 0 3rem}.book-card{grid-template-columns:38px minmax(0,1fr)}.book-content{padding:1.3rem}.intro-columns{gap:1rem}}
  @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.game-card,.book-card,.poetry-grid :global(.poem),.library-index a{transition:none;transform:none!important}}
</style>
